  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146616",
      "title": "Introducing State",
      "lectureOrder": 63,
      "videoOrder": 59,
      "sourceHash": "bc3d00ce83f92185a517de227c05788536e55e15ab1764ae726e5996468d733e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.47,
          "en": "In order to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.47,
          "end": 4.87,
          "en": "what's visible on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.87,
          "end": 8.14,
          "en": "we need to change the state of this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.14,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 12.45,
          "en": "Now, attached you find an extra article and video",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.45,
          "end": 13.36,
          "en": "which I created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 13.36,
          "end": 16.17,
          "en": "where I explain what state is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 18.529,
          "en": "In the end, you can take it quite literally though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.529,
          "end": 20.86,
          "en": "The current state of this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.86,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "is that we have free Todos and this overlay is open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.53,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "Now, we would like to also be able to present",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 33.2,
          "en": "another state, where this overlay is closed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.2,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "And we want to switch between the states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 38.39,
          "en": "When we click on delete, then it should open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.39,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "And when we click on cancel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 41.71,
          "en": "or confirm or the backdrop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.71,
          "end": 43.25,
          "en": "it should close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.25,
          "end": 46.63,
          "en": "So that should be our ways of switching between the states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.63,
          "end": 49.99,
          "en": "and React has a built in concept that helps us with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.99,
          "end": 53.28,
          "en": "And conveniently, it's called State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.28,
          "end": 57.17,
          "en": "For this, let's go to our Todo.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.17,
          "end": 58.64,
          "en": "to our Todo component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.64,
          "end": 60.5,
          "en": "Here, we got this delete handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.5,
          "end": 62.03,
          "en": "this function which is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.03,
          "end": 64.15,
          "en": "when the delete button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.15,
          "end": 67.16,
          "en": "When it is clicked, we would like to switch to the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.16,
          "end": 69.19,
          "en": "where the modal is open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 69.19,
          "end": 72.676,
          "en": "To make that happen, we need to import some functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.676,
          "end": 75.89,
          "en": "from the React library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 75.89,
          "end": 77.98,
          "en": "So we import from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.98,
          "end": 78.97,
          "en": "Import here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 78.97,
          "end": 80.68,
          "en": "We have no dot slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.68,
          "end": 83.18,
          "en": "because React is a third party library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 83.18,
          "end": 87.253,
          "en": "You import from those by just referencing the library name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.1,
          "end": 91,
          "en": "And then we import something like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 91,
          "end": 92.56,
          "en": "with curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 92.56,
          "end": 96.06,
          "en": "We import the useState function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 96.06,
          "end": 99.77000000000001,
          "en": "That is a function exposed by the React library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 99.77000000000001,
          "end": 102.68299999999999,
          "en": "which we can use in our component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.52000000000001,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "With useState, we register different States,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 111.28999999999999,
          "en": "which we want to support in our React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.28999999999999,
          "end": 114.406,
          "en": "and React will react to changes in that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.406,
          "end": 118.686,
          "en": "and allow us as a developer to render different output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.686,
          "end": 121.6,
          "en": "depending on which State is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.6,
          "end": 124.72,
          "en": "Now, that all starts with calling useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.72,
          "end": 128.21,
          "en": "directly in our component function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.21,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "So not inside of delete handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 132.753,
          "en": "instead, directly in the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 133.669,
          "end": 136.9,
          "en": "UseState is a so-called React hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.9,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "and those React hooks can only be called directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 144.307,
          "en": "in React component functions and in custom hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.307,
          "end": 147.32,
          "en": "which is a topic will not discuss in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.32,
          "end": 151.3,
          "en": "but which is discussed in depth in my complete guide as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.3,
          "end": 153.21,
          "en": "For the moment it's enough that we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.21,
          "end": 158.06,
          "en": "that we can use React Hooks in React component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.06,
          "end": 161.7,
          "en": "Now, calling useState creates a state React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 161.7,
          "end": 162.87,
          "en": "as a wear ofF.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.87,
          "end": 165.77,
          "en": "Now, we can give this state a starting value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.77,
          "end": 168.61599999999999,
          "en": "by passing it here as an argument to useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.61599999999999,
          "end": 172.23,
          "en": "And that could be false if our state is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.23,
          "end": 175.696,
          "en": "that we want to control whether the modal is open or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.696,
          "end": 178.24,
          "en": "and initially, it should not be open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.24,
          "end": 180.54,
          "en": "So the initial state is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.54,
          "end": 185.02,
          "en": "Now, useState always returns an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.02,
          "end": 187.66,
          "en": "with exactly two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 187.66,
          "end": 189.17,
          "en": "That's how useState works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 189.17,
          "end": 192.56,
          "en": "It always returns an array with two elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.56,
          "end": 195.55,
          "en": "and we can store it as returned array in a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.55,
          "end": 198.37,
          "en": "or we use array de-structuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 198.37,
          "end": 202.61,
          "en": "which is a JavaScript feature to store these two elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 202.61,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "since we know that it will be always two elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 207.505,
          "en": "indifferent constants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 207.505,
          "end": 211.793,
          "en": "and we could give to first constant a name of showModal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.76,
          "end": 215.906,
          "en": "or modalIsOpen open or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 215.906,
          "end": 219.88,
          "en": "And the second element here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 219.88,
          "end": 221.28,
          "en": "the second constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 222.53,
          "en": "a name of setModalIsOpen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.39,
          "end": 226.62,
          "en": "Now, why did I choose these names?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.62,
          "end": 228.94,
          "en": "Because the first element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.94,
          "end": 231.299,
          "en": "which useState returns in its array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.299,
          "end": 234.29,
          "en": "is the current state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.29,
          "end": 238.04,
          "en": "So this value, which is stored in this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.04,
          "end": 241,
          "en": "You can think of React state as a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241,
          "end": 243.9,
          "en": "which is managed for you by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 243.9,
          "end": 246.01,
          "en": "You define the initial value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.01,
          "end": 248.98,
          "en": "and you will then also be able to change that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 248.98,
          "end": 251.37,
          "en": "Now, you get access to the currently stored value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 254.07,
          "en": "for this first element here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 254.07,
          "end": 255.33,
          "en": "The second element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 255.33,
          "end": 258.92,
          "en": "is a function that allows you to change that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 258.92,
          "end": 260.21,
          "en": "because you don't change it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 260.21,
          "end": 263.12,
          "en": "by assigning a new value to modalIsOpen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 263.12,
          "end": 266.33,
          "en": "instead, you always call this second function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 266.33,
          "end": 268.9,
          "en": "to assign a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 268.9,
          "end": 270.28,
          "en": "Why does this matter?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 270.28,
          "end": 273.501,
          "en": "Because whenever you call this state changing function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 273.501,
          "end": 277.1,
          "en": "React will in the end re-execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 277.1,
          "end": 280.64,
          "en": "the component function to which this state belongs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 280.64,
          "end": 282.74,
          "en": "and re-evaluate it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 282.74,
          "end": 285.97,
          "en": "and also update what's rendered on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 285.97,
          "end": 289.52,
          "en": "This allows you to pick up the latest state value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 289.52,
          "end": 291.76,
          "en": "and possibly render something different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 291.76,
          "end": 293.9,
          "en": "depending on the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 293.9,
          "end": 296.21,
          "en": "Notice it might still be a bit abstract.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 296.21,
          "end": 299.37,
          "en": "It will become crystal clear in a couple of seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 299.37,
          "end": 302.46,
          "en": "What we can do now with these two elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 302.46,
          "end": 303.989,
          "en": "is that in delete handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 303.989,
          "end": 307.94,
          "en": "we call setModalIsOpen and set is to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 307.94,
          "end": 311.13,
          "en": "To change that modalIsOpen state from false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 311.13,
          "end": 313.848,
          "en": "which is our initial state, to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 313.848,
          "end": 316.034,
          "en": "And then we use modalIsOpen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 316.034,
          "end": 319.57,
          "en": "to conditionally render the modal and backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 319.57,
          "end": 321.673,
          "en": "down there in this JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 327.01,
          "en": "So I go to App.js and I remove modal and backdrop from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 327.01,
          "end": 328.73,
          "en": "and remove the imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 328.73,
          "end": 331.23,
          "en": "since we're not using modal and backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 331.23,
          "end": 332.913,
          "en": "in this file anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 333.81,
          "end": 336.14,
          "en": "And instead I'll go to Todo.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 336.14,
          "end": 340.469,
          "en": "and import modal there from ./Modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 340.469,
          "end": 344.969,
          "en": "and import backdrop here from ./Backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 344.969,
          "end": 348.61,
          "en": "Constructing the relative paths to these files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 348.61,
          "end": 352.2,
          "en": "as seen from inside this Todo.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 352.2,
          "end": 355.5,
          "en": "And since modal and backdrop are neighbors to this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 355.5,
          "end": 357.28,
          "en": "the paths look just like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 358.12,
          "end": 360.33,
          "en": "and then we can use these components down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 360.33,
          "end": 362.59,
          "en": "Let's say here in that div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 362.59,
          "end": 365.363,
          "en": "Modal and Backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 366.27,
          "end": 369.75,
          "en": "Now, if we added like this, they would always be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 369.75,
          "end": 371.23,
          "en": "I only want to render them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 371.23,
          "end": 373.24,
          "en": "if modalIsOpen is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 373.24,
          "end": 375.94,
          "en": "If that state has a value of true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 375.94,
          "end": 377.484,
          "en": "Now, we are changing the state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 377.484,
          "end": 379.11,
          "en": "To use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 379.11,
          "end": 382.629,
          "en": "we can simply output a dynamic expression down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 382.629,
          "end": 387.31,
          "en": "and check if modalIsOpen is truth like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 387.31,
